<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">appraise</ansi>

The <ansi fg="command">appraise</ansi> command pays a merchant to
reveal the properties of an item in your backpack.

<ansi fg="yellow">Usage: </ansi>

::keep
  <ansi fg="command">appraise sword</ansi>
::

Costs 20 gold per item. You must be in a room with a
merchant.

Small found trinkets (baubles) are appraised for free: the
merchant tells you what it is made of, what it weighs, where
it came from, and what they would pay for it.

If you know the <ansi fg="spellname">identify</ansi> spell, you
can examine items anywhere without a merchant. See
<ansi fg="command">help identify</ansi>.

::rows
<ansi fg="magenta-bold">See also:</ansi>  <ansi fg="command">help identify</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help inventory</ansi>
::

